  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given an array AAA, which is a permutation of the integers [1,N][1, N][1,N].\n\nYour task is to sort the array using the following operations as many times as you want:\n\n\nChoose an index iii (1≤i≤N1 \\le i \\le N1≤i≤N), and then pay AiA_iAi​ coins to sort the prefix A[1,i]A[1, i]A[1,i] of the array. (Note that the cost is levied before the sorting operation is performed)\nHere, A[1,i]A[1, i]A[1,i] represents the prefix [A1,A2,…,Ai][A_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_i][A1​,A2​,…,Ai​].\n\nWhat is the minimum total cost to sort the array?\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line contains a single integer NNN.\nThe second line contains NNN integers - A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the minimum cost to sort the array.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1001 \\le T \\le 1001≤T≤100",
      "1≤N≤1001 \\le N \\le 1001≤N≤100",
      "1≤Ai≤N1 \\le A_i \\le N1≤Ai​≤N",
      "Ai≠AjA_i \\ne A_jAi​=Aj​ for all i≠ji \\ne ji=j."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
